cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code for archaeal MAGs from the deep Gulf of Mexico
message: If you use this code, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Castañeda-Martínez
    given-names: Rubén
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9272-7968"
    affiliation: >-
      Centro de Investigación Científica y de Educación Superior de Ensenada
      (CICESE)
version: "0.0.1"
repository-code: https://github.com/ruben1294/gom-archaeal-mags
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Pipeline and analysis code for 54 archaeal metagenome-assembled genomes from
  six stations and three depths in the deep Gulf of Mexico. Covers quality
  assessment and chimerism screening, GTDB taxonomic classification, functional
  annotation with DRAM2 and eggNOG-mapper, marker-based phylogenomics, ANI, and
  anvi'o pangenomics across the species with enough genomes to support it. The
  MAGs come from the contig assembly and binning of Osorio Pando (2025).
keywords:
  - archaea
  - metagenome-assembled genomes
  - Gulf of Mexico
  - phylogenomics
  - pangenomics
  - functional annotation
  - Poseidoniales
  - Nitrososphaerales
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: >-
      Estructura y función de las comunidades de bacterias y arqueas en las
      zonas mesopelágica y batipelágica del golfo de México
    authors:
      - family-names: Osorio Pando
        given-names: Lizt Selene Sibila
    year: 2025
    thesis-type: >-
      Doctoral thesis, Doctorado en Ciencias en Ciencias de la Vida con
      orientación en Microbiología
    institution:
      name: >-
        Centro de Investigación Científica y de Educación Superior de Ensenada,
        Baja California (CICESE)
      city: Ensenada
      country: MX
    notes: >-
      Contig assembly and binning of the MAGs analysed here, and the source of
      the environmental tables in data/ (its Tablas 2 and 9).
